 "narr": {
  "Aqua Shard": "W35 users 26,243 (-4.0% YoY) with 1,244 GA4 bookings (-30.6% YoY); conversion rate 4.7% vs 6.6% LY. Google delivered 273 bookings at £9 CPA; Meta 243 at £11. Modelled store visits for the last two weeks are still settling upward, so treat the latest walk-in point as provisional.",
  "Hutong": "W35 users 17,739 (+7.7% YoY) with 1,004 GA4 bookings (+13.7% YoY); conversion rate 5.7% vs 5.4% LY. Google delivered 257 bookings at £8 CPA; Meta 188 at £12. This is its best booking week since late August. Modelled store visits for the last two weeks are still settling upward, so treat the latest walk-in point as provisional.",
  "Regent St": "W35 users 3,829 (-45.6% YoY) with 201 GA4 bookings (-30.9% YoY); conversion rate 5.2% vs 4.1% LY. Google delivered 7 bookings at £75 CPA; Meta 53 at £15. This account has no modelled store visits, so the walk-in panel is directions, menu views and calls only. Last year's four weeks were an unusually busy spell on the Kyoto site, which exaggerates the traffic drop.",
  "Azzurra": "W35 users 2,580 (+23.3% YoY) with 116 GA4 bookings (+14.9% YoY); conversion rate 4.5% vs 4.8% LY. Google delivered 11 bookings at £47 CPA; Meta 76 at £18. An email send worth 640 sessions is what pushed traffic above last year. This account has no modelled store visits in 2026, so the walk-in panel is directions, menu views and calls only, and last year's panel is store visits only.",
  "Shiro Sushi": "W35 users 1,347 (-29.1% YoY) with 97 GA4 bookings (-10.2% YoY); conversion rate 7.2% vs 5.7% LY. Google delivered 23 bookings at £24 CPA; Meta 40 at £13. Google had published only eight modelled store visits for this week when the data was pulled, so the latest walk-in point understates the true figure.",
  "DSL": "W35 users 5,775 (+298.0% YoY) with 478 GA4 bookings (+368.6% YoY); conversion rate 8.3% vs 7.0% LY. Meta spend of £2,297 produced 116 schedules and Google £321 produced 10 booking conversions; DSL has no 2025 Google history at all, so last year reads as zero on the Google panels. The account records no Google walk-in actions, so that panel is empty by fact."
